## Why This Is Asked

Tests reasoning with Kleene 3-valued logic on implications and disjunctions, plus a concrete backtracking strategy that preserves non-F constraints while allowing Unknowns.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued semantics
- Implication as ¬A ∨ B
- Propagation and pruning in backtracking
- Constructing a concrete satisfying assignment with U

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal 3-valued logic helpers
const order = {F:0, U:1, T:2};
function not(v){ return v==='T'?'F':v==='F'?'T':'U';}
function or(a,b){ return order[a] >= order[b] ? a : b; }
function and(a,b){ return order[a] <= order[b] ? a : b; }
function implies(a,b){ return or(not(a), b); }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to detect unsatisfiable constraint sets with a fixed number of U?
- How would you implement a backtracking search that guarantees termination in finite time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests design of a constraint solver for non-classical logics with custom operators and propagation strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Kleene three-valued semantics (T > U > F)
- Custom operators →* (strong implication) and ⊕ (parity)
- Forward checking, variable ordering, and backtracking in non-deterministic domains

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Kleene 3-valued semantics (T=1, U=0, F=-1)
const T=1, U=0, F=-1;
function not(v){ return v===T?F : v===F?T : U; }
function kleeneAnd(a,b){ if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return T; }
function kleeneOr(a,b){ if(a===T||b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F; }
function strongImpl(a,b){ // placeholder behavior for demonstration
  if(a===F) return T; if(a===T) return b; return (b===F?F:(b===U?U:T));
}
function parity(a,b){ // placeholder: U propagates unless forced by T/F
  if(a===F||b===F) return F; if(a===T&&b===T) return T; if(a===U||b===U) return U; return F;
}
```

